# Keybind labels for Mod+K (hexciri-keybinds) — one per line:
#
#   Mod+Ctrl+D = Vesktop
#   Mod+Shift+W = Browser (private)
#
# Combo matching is case-insensitive and whitespace-tolerant (`mod+ctrl+d`
# matches `Mod+Ctrl+D`). `#` comments and blank lines are ignored. Either `=`
# or `:` separates the combo from the label (first one wins).
#
# Your copy at ~/.config/hexciri/keybinds/descriptions.list adds to / overrides
# this shipped file, and both override the builtin core labels. Anything not
# listed anywhere falls back to the builtin core labels, then to a prettified
# spawn (first command only, deduped — e.g. spawn "vesktop" "vesktop" → vesktop,
# hexciri webapp launchers → their app name).
#
# So most custom binds (like the Vesktop one above) already read sensibly with
# zero config — this file is for the ones where you want your own wording.
#
# Examples (uncomment to use):
# Mod+Ctrl+D = Vesktop
# Mod+Shift+W = Browser (private)
